  "subtitle": "the toy drum machine that Kraftwerk took seriously",
  "why_scout_cares": "Hybrid manual/automatic interface: play with sticks OR program patterns with auto-repeat buttons OR layer both in real time. A toy company made an all-analog drum synth with velocity-sensitive pads and a tap-tempo microprocessor, and professional musicians adopted it. The bass drum can only be played automatically — a design choice that reveals the ambiguous identity between toy and instrument. Distinct from every existing music exhibit: no other collection artifact fuses stick-pad drumming, auto-sequencing, and analog synthesis in a single handheld box.",
